    "Every case is isolated and has no dependency on another case.",
    "Calibration and validation families do not paraphrase one another.",
    "At least half of cases contain a tempting but unauthorized inference.",
    "At least one quarter contain a genuine user-owned decision.",
    "At least one quarter are fully actionable despite superficial ambiguity.",
    "Keys describe meaning; they do not prescribe one universal interaction style.",
    "Free reconstruction is retained alongside structured fields and any later scores."
    ,"Equivalent variants preserve the interpretation key while changing one linguistic factor."
    ,"Contrast variants change one semantic operator and receive a different interpretation key."
    ,"Format preference is inferred from accuracy and stability, never from self-reported preference alone."
